---
T1.8 (#1021): `NonEmpty` and `MinLength(1)` are the same refinement spelled
differently. Before the fold this fixture would raise
`bynk.boundary.structural_mismatch` — same shape as
`negative/80_structural_mismatch`, but for a Refined pair rather than a
Record field-name mismatch — because `refinements_match` compared canonical
forms that differed only in spelling. After the fold both sides canonicalise
to `MinLength(1)` and this compiles clean.
---
context boundary.consumer

consumes boundary.provider as Provider

type LocalToken = String where MinLength(1)

service submit {
  on call(value: LocalToken) -> Effect[Result[Int, Int]] {
    let _ <- Provider.verify(value)
    Effect.pure(Ok(0))
  }
}
